  id: W1_02
  era: "c. 2000\u20131900 BCE"
  title: The 'Priest-King'
  text: "The 'Priest-King'. Found at Mohenjo-daro in the mid-1920s, this bearded man wears a band around his head and a robe decorated with trefoil patterns that were once filled with red paste. Archaeologists nicknamed him the 'Priest-King', but nobody knows who he really was \u2013 the Indus script has never been deciphered. Mohenjo-daro was one of the largest cities of the Bronze Age world, with tens of thousands of people living in streets laid out on a grid, with covered drains and brick houses. Yet it has no grand palaces or royal tombs, which is one reason its rulers remain a mystery."
  narration: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 40b62b65bbfed48899bdb85911e8a659, type: 3}
